  "description": "UPIXID crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H80 N34 Na2 O16 Yb4. From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 5 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 4 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 5 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.769-4.121 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.43-121.66°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C88H80Yb4N34Na2O16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
